  "gaps": [
    "The BS in Marketing table prints only a combined 51-credit block for remaining general education and electives; it does not state how those 51 credits split between general education and electives. Arithmetic from the 41-credit general education total minus the 15 business-core credits that 'may be applied to general education requirements' suggests about 26 general education and 25 elective credits, but this split is not printed.",
    "The remaining general education sub-blocks are listed in the generic requirements and are not restated for this major: WRTG 111 or another writing course (3), a communication/writing/speech course (3), an upper-level advanced writing course (3), Arts and Humanities (6), Biological and Physical Sciences (7), a professional exploration course (3), and LIBS 150/CAPL 398A or another 1-credit course (1).",
    "Residency rules are stated only as aggregate policies, not tied to specific courses: at least 30 credits (normally the final 30) at UMGC, half of the major credits at UMGC, and at least 15 upper-level (300–499) credits at UMGC. Because no course is named, no requirement is flagged institutionalOnly.",
    "The MRKT 210 alternative 'or any MRKT course' could overlap with other MRKT requirements. The capture does not say whether one course may satisfy more than one major requirement within a single major.",
    "The course sequencing table is a recommendation (for example, PACE 111B, LIBS 150, WRTG 111, SPCH 100, NUTR 100, BIOL 103, HUMN 100, ARTH 334, WRTG 394, CAPL 398A). The capture does not state that these specific courses are mandatory."
  ],
